            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "GNC lists 40 g of protein per two-scoop serving, about 20 g per scoop. The Natural Chocolate and Natural Vanilla tubs list about 220 calories per serving and about 25 servings per container, and the Ripped version lists about 200 calories with about 22 servings, at the time of writing. Check your tub, since figures vary by flavor."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is AMP Wheybolic better than Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not on protein quality. Both are good whey proteins, and Gold Standard's 24 g scoop is simply smaller than Wheybolic's 40 g two-scoop serving. Gold Standard usually costs less per 25 g of protein on Amazon and promotes Informed Choice certification on many flavors. AMP Wheybolic can win on price during GNC sales."
          }
        },
