        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing grams per serving instead of per gram</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                AMP Wheybolic's 40 g serving is two scoops, so a tub of 25 servings holds the same protein as a tub of 40 servings at 25 g. Always divide the price by total grams of protein and multiply by 25. That is the only fair way to compare it with other whey.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying full price at GNC</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                GNC's shelf prices are often high, but the chain runs frequent sales, bundles and member deals. Buying AMP Wheybolic at regular price usually makes it more expensive per gram than mainstream whey on Amazon. Wait for a promotion, or buy a rival that is cheaper on the day.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Using two scoops by default</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Most people get most of the muscle-building benefit of a meal from around 20 to 25 g of protein. Two scoops adds about 100 calories and halves the life of the tub. Start with one scoop and use two only after big full-body sessions or if you need the extra protein to hit your daily target.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming third-party tested means certified</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A listing that says third-party tested is not the same as NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport, which screen for banned substances. If you compete under drug testing, choose a product that appears in a certifier's database and check the exact flavor and batch before you buy.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating the shake as your main protein</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The ready-to-drink AMP Wheybolic 40 has a strong label, but bottled shakes cost far more per gram than powder. Keep a few for travel and busy days and get your everyday protein from food and powder. Anyone with kidney disease should check high-protein products with a doctor.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
